  "solution": {
    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/8585415841.JPG\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 208px;\" /><br /><br />where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>θ</mi></math><br /><br />at time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>, in Uniform circular motion only&nbsp;centripetal force exists&nbsp;constant in magnitude<br /><br />So, Y - component of force is <math>&nbsp;<mo>⇒</mo><mover accent=\"true\"> <mrow> <msub><mtext>F</mtext><mtext>y</mtext></msub> </mrow> <mo stretchy=\"true\">→</mo> </mover> <mtext> </mtext><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mtext>F</mtext><mtext>sin</mtext><mtext>θ</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mover accent=\"true\"> <mtext>j</mtext> <mo stretchy=\"true\">^</mo> </mover> </math><br /><br /><math> <msub><mtext>F</mtext><mtext>y</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mtext>F</mtext><mtext>sin</mtext><mtext>ω</mtext><mtext>t</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mover accent=\"true\"> <mtext>j</mtext> <mo stretchy=\"true\">^</mo> </mover> </math> (as, <!-- MathType@Translator@5@5@MathML2 (namespace attr).tdl@MathML 2.0 (namespace attr)@ --> <math> <mrow> <mtext>θ</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>ωt</mtext></mrow> </math> <!-- MathType@End@5@5@ --> )<br /><br />So given graph is correct for <math><msub><mtext>F</mtext><mtext>y</mtext></msub></math> vs <math><mtext>t</mtext></math><br /><br />In Uniform circular motion.&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mtext>V</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac> <mtext>ω</mtext> <mtext>r</mtext> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> </mrow> </math> &nbsp;constant<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/59654964196.JPG\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 215px;\" /><br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/416418541.JPG\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 190px;\" /><br /><br /><math> <mo>⇒</mo><mover accent=\"true\"> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>V</mtext> <mtext>x</mtext> </msub> </mrow> <mo stretchy=\"true\">→</mo> </mover> <mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mtext>V</mtext><mtext>sin</mtext><mtext>ω</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>t</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mover accent=\"true\"> <mtext>j</mtext> <mo stretchy=\"true\">^</mo> </mover></math><br /><br />So given graph for <math> <msub> <mtext>V</mtext> <mtext>x</mtext> </msub> <mo>−</mo><mtext>t</mtext> </math>&nbsp;is incorrect.<br /><br />In Uniform circular motion.,&nbsp; &nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mtext>ω</mtext><mo>=</mo> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;constant<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>∴</mo><mtext> </mtext><mtext>ω</mtext><mo>−</mo><mtext>t</mtext> </mrow> </math> &nbsp; graph is correct<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/8418541796.JPG\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 173px;\" /><br /><br /><math> <mo>∵</mo><mtext> </mtext><mtext>x</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>r</mtext><mtext>cos</mtext><mtext>θ</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext> </mtext><mtext>r</mtext><mtext>cos</mtext><mtext>ω</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>t</mtext> </math><br /><br /><math> <mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mtext>x</mtext><mo>−</mo><mtext>t</mtext> </math>&nbsp; graph is correct",
